  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>In multi-electronic species, energy is decided on the basis of (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></math>) rule.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>6</mn></math></p><p>For 4s and 3p, an orbital with a higher value of n has higher energy.</p><p>So increasing the order of energy is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>.</p>"
  }
}